NEW BUG FOUND - add to the list
[ ] P0/P1 Shell env leak
    The integrated terminal passes Dovee's own server environment into every user shell:
      NODE_ENV=production
      TURBOPACK=1
      PORT=3100
      __NEXT_PRIVATE_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:3100
      __NEXT_PRIVATE_STANDALONE_CONFIG={... "outputFileTracingRoot": "...\Dovee\resources\standalone" ...}
      TURBO_CACHE_DIR=...
    Effect: running `npm run dev` inside Dovee's terminal is broken:
      - "non-standard NODE_ENV" warning, dev runs in a production-ish mode
      - `next dev --webpack` fails: "Multiple bundler flags set: TURBOPACK=1, --webpack"
      - module resolution points at the INSTALLED APP directory instead of the project,
        so packages resolve as bogus hashed names (this is what made a native dep look
        like a Turbopack bug)
    Fix: strip __NEXT_PRIVATE_*, NODE_ENV, TURBOPACK, PORT, TURBO_CACHE_DIR when building
    env in spawnShell() (src/lib/shell.ts).


